# Branch and file naming (synthetic fixture)

This file is intentionally long so the Switchboard preview truncation is exercised by the
fixture instead of by a hand written string in the test.

Rule 01: name branches by intent, not by ticket alone.
Rule 02: one component per file, file named after the component.
Rule 03: hooks live next to the component that uses them.
Rule 04: no barrel files at the root of a package.
Rule 05: tests sit under a tests directory, mirroring src.
Rule 06: keep the design tokens in one place and reference them.
Rule 07: never hard code a color in a component.
Rule 08: never hard code a duration in a component.
Rule 09: prefer a plain function over a class with one method.
Rule 10: prefer an explicit error type over a thrown string.
Rule 11: keep parse and render separate so each is testable.
Rule 12: no network calls inside render.
Rule 13: no secrets in source, even fake ones from a fixture.
Rule 14: mask anything that looks like a key before showing it.
Rule 15: if a value is a reference to an environment variable, show the name only.
Rule 16: a rules preview is a preview, not a full file copy.
Rule 17: show the path so the user can go read the real file.
Rule 18: differences between agents are the point of this view.
Rule 19: an absent file is information, not an error.
Rule 20: when two agents agree, say so plainly and get out of the way.
